# How to use the Multi Camera Multi Object Tracking System:

The Framework is composed of various scripts.
1- train.py 
    If you want to train a new model you can execute this script. Remember to respect the YOLO dataset expectations of train, test, validation folders with the images and labels inside.

2- multicamera.yaml 
    When implementing this script on a different dataset or application, where there are more classes, this script should be modified to represent that.

3- pipeline.py
    If you are working with recorded streams, remember to save them in a folder inside MCMOT_TFG/models/dataset/videos/
    When launching the system do:
        python pipeline.py
    From a folder parent to MCMOT_TFG.

    The videos writen in the scripts "SOURCES" will be used as the input of the pipeline. The output of the pipeline will end in MCMOT_TFG/models/output/"folder_name"

    The YOLO model used is chosen from those trained or downloaded and stored in MCMOT_TFG/models/scripts/runs/detect/...

The rest of the scripts can be altered to modify parameters according to the needs of the user but otherwise should not be touched.

